IMPORT types

-- Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ)
-- Part 1 -- Preliminary provisions (cll 1 to 10).
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/LMS1592864.xml, 2026 No 339-1, retrieved 2026-09-11.

§ `Part 1 -- Preliminary provisions`

§§ `1. Title, 2. Commencement`

`the short title of this Act` MEANS "Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Act 2026"

-- cl 2: this Act comes into force 6 months after Royal assent.
`months after Royal assent before commencement` MEANS 6

§§ `3. Purpose`

-- cl 3: the purpose of this Act is to reduce the risk of harm to children when
-- online by imposing duties on operators of certain internet services.
-- Encoded as a constant: the purpose bears on cl 7(1) (the regulator may
-- designate only if satisfied that doing so promotes this purpose) and on
-- cll 61 to 63, but it is not itself a determination.

`the purpose of this Act` MEANS "to reduce the risk of harm to children when online by imposing duties on operators of certain internet services"

§§ `5. Meaning of age-restricted platform`

-- cl 5(2): specified feature, in relation to an internet service, means a
-- feature that recommends content based on the user, generates a continuously
-- updated stream, displays engagement information about user content, enables
-- time-limited engagement, or is specified in regulations.

GIVEN s IS A `internet service`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the service has 1 or more specified features` IF
        s's `recommends digital content to a user based on information about that user`
    OR  s's `generates a continuously updated stream of digital content`
    OR  s's `displays information about how others have viewed or engaged with user content`
    OR  s's `enables a user to view or engage with digital content for a limited period`
    OR  s's `has a feature specified as a specified feature in regulations under section 62`

-- cl 5(2): excluded service means an internet service that solely or primarily
-- enables a user to do any of eight listed activities, regardless of whether it
-- meets the criteria in cl 5(1)(a)(ii) and (iii).

GIVEN s IS A `internet service`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the service is an excluded service` IF
        s's `solely or primarily enables person-to-person messages, email, voice or video calls`
    OR  s's `solely or primarily enables video gaming`
    OR  s's `solely or primarily enables access to music or podcasts on demand`
    OR  s's `solely or primarily enables access to reviews, technical support, or advice`
    OR  s's `solely or primarily enables professional networking or development`
    OR  s's `solely or primarily enables access to or engagement in education services`
    OR  s's `solely or primarily enables access to or engagement in healthcare services`
    OR  s's `solely or primarily enables an activity specified in regulations under section 62`

-- cl 5(1)(a): the four-limb conjunctive test, including the excluded-service carve-out.

GIVEN s IS A `internet service`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the service is an age-restricted platform under section 5(1)(a)` IF
        s's `is accessible by a person who is in New Zealand`
    AND s's `enables the exchange of digital content between 2 or more users`
    AND `the service has 1 or more specified features` s
    AND NOT `the service is an excluded service` s

-- cl 5(1)(b): the AI companion limb. Note that it carries NO excluded-service
-- carve-out and requires no specified feature -- see NOTES.md, #1.

GIVEN s IS A `internet service`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the service is an age-restricted platform under section 5(1)(b)` IF
        s's `is accessible by a person who is in New Zealand`
    AND s's `displays or otherwise makes available digital content`
    AND s's `uses artificial intelligence solely or primarily to simulate a personal connection`

-- cl 5(1)(c): the regulation-making limb.

GIVEN s IS A `internet service`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the service is an age-restricted platform under section 5(1)(c)` IF
    s's `is specified as an age-restricted platform in regulations under section 62`

@ref Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ) cl 5
@export Decide whether an internet service is an age-restricted platform within the meaning of clause 5
GIVEN s IS A `internet service` @desc The clause 5 facts for the service: New Zealand accessibility, exchange between users, which specified features it has, which excluded-service activity it solely or primarily enables, whether it is an AI companion service, and whether regulations name it.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the service is an age-restricted platform` IF
        `the service is an age-restricted platform under section 5(1)(a)` s
    OR  `the service is an age-restricted platform under section 5(1)(b)` s
    OR  `the service is an age-restricted platform under section 5(1)(c)` s

§§ `6. Meaning of operator, 7. Regulator's power to designate operators`

-- cl 6(1): operator, in respect of an age-restricted platform, means a person
-- that, directly or indirectly by any means, manages or controls the platform's
-- operations in New Zealand (whether by itself or together with other persons).

GIVEN p IS A `person in relation to platform`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is an operator under section 6(1)` IF
    p's `manages or controls the operations of the platform in New Zealand`

-- cl 7(2): without limiting cl 7(1), designating a person will promote the
-- purpose of this Act if the designation is necessary or desirable to provide
-- certainty about who is and is not an operator, or to ensure that this Act can
-- be effectively enforced in respect of the platform. The limb is inclusive, so
-- the regulator's own satisfaction under cl 7(1) is an independent route.

GIVEN p IS A `person in relation to platform`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `designating the person promotes the purpose of this Act` IF
        p's `designating provides certainty about who is and is not an operator`
    OR  p's `designating ensures this Act can be effectively enforced for the platform`
    OR  p's `the regulator is satisfied that designating this person promotes the purpose`

@ref Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ) cl 7(1)
GIVEN p IS A `person in relation to platform`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the regulator may designate the person as the operator` IF
        `designating the person promotes the purpose of this Act` p
    AND (    `the person is an operator under section 6(1)` p
          OR p's `is an interconnected body corporate of an operator under section 6(1)` )

-- cl 6(2): if the regulator has designated a person as the operator under cl 7,
-- that person is the ONLY operator for the purposes of this Act while the
-- designation is in place. A cl 6(1) manager or controller is therefore
-- displaced by a live designation of someone else -- see NOTES.md, #6.

@ref Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ) cl 6
@export Decide whether a person is the operator of an age-restricted platform for the purposes of the Act
GIVEN p IS A `person in relation to platform` @desc The clause 6 facts for the person: whether they manage or control the operations of the platform in New Zealand, whether a section 7 designation is in place for the platform at all, and whether this person is the one designated.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is the operator of the platform` IF
    IF   p's `a designation under section 7 is in place for the platform`
    THEN p's `has been designated by the regulator as the operator under section 7`
    ELSE `the person is an operator under section 6(1)` p

§§ `8. Territorial application`

-- cl 8: this Act applies to an operator regardless of whether the operator is in
-- or outside New Zealand, but only to the extent that the platform is operated
-- in a manner that enables a person who is in New Zealand to access it. The
-- location of the operator is therefore not a condition, and is not modelled.

@ref Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ) cl 8
@export Decide whether the Act applies to a person as operator of an age-restricted platform
GIVEN p IS A `person in relation to platform` @desc The clause 6 facts, plus whether the platform is operated so as to enable access by a person who is in New Zealand.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this Act applies to the person as operator of the platform` IF
        `the person is the operator of the platform` p
    AND p's `the platform is operated so as to enable a person who is in New Zealand to access it`

§§ `9. Transitional provisions, 10. Act binds the Crown`

-- cl 9: the transitional, savings, and related provisions in Schedule 1 have
-- effect according to their terms. Encoded in schedule-1-transitional.l4.

-- cl 10: this Act binds the Crown.
`this Act binds the Crown` MEANS TRUE

§§ `Scenario fixtures`

-- An ordinary social platform: caught by limb (a).
`a social feed platform` MEANS `internet service` WITH
    name                                                                                IS "SocialFeed"
    `is accessible by a person who is in New Zealand`                                    IS TRUE
    `enables the exchange of digital content between 2 or more users`                    IS TRUE
    `recommends digital content to a user based on information about that user`          IS TRUE
    `generates a continuously updated stream of digital content`                         IS TRUE
    `displays information about how others have viewed or engaged with user content`     IS TRUE
    `enables a user to view or engage with digital content for a limited period`         IS FALSE
    `has a feature specified as a specified feature in regulations under section 62`     IS FALSE
    `solely or primarily enables person-to-person messages, email, voice or video calls` IS FALSE
    `solely or primarily enables video gaming`                                           IS FALSE
    `solely or primarily enables access to music or podcasts on demand`                  IS FALSE
    `solely or primarily enables access to reviews, technical support, or advice`        IS FALSE
    `solely or primarily enables professional networking or development`                 IS FALSE
    `solely or primarily enables access to or engagement in education services`          IS FALSE
    `solely or primarily enables access to or engagement in healthcare services`         IS FALSE
    `solely or primarily enables an activity specified in regulations under section 62`  IS FALSE
    `displays or otherwise makes available digital content`                              IS TRUE
    `uses artificial intelligence solely or primarily to simulate a personal connection` IS FALSE
    `is specified as an age-restricted platform in regulations under section 62`         IS FALSE

-- A therapy chatbot: solely or primarily a healthcare service, so excluded from
-- limb (a) -- but it is an AI companion, and limb (b) has no carve-out.
`a therapy chatbot` MEANS `internet service` WITH
    name                                                                                IS "TherapyBot"
    `is accessible by a person who is in New Zealand`                                    IS TRUE
    `enables the exchange of digital content between 2 or more users`                    IS FALSE
    `recommends digital content to a user based on information about that user`          IS TRUE
    `generates a continuously updated stream of digital content`                         IS FALSE
    `displays information about how others have viewed or engaged with user content`     IS FALSE
    `enables a user to view or engage with digital content for a limited period`         IS FALSE
    `has a feature specified as a specified feature in regulations under section 62`     IS FALSE
    `solely or primarily enables person-to-person messages, email, voice or video calls` IS FALSE
    `solely or primarily enables video gaming`                                           IS FALSE
    `solely or primarily enables access to music or podcasts on demand`                  IS FALSE
    `solely or primarily enables access to reviews, technical support, or advice`        IS FALSE
    `solely or primarily enables professional networking or development`                 IS FALSE
    `solely or primarily enables access to or engagement in education services`          IS FALSE
    `solely or primarily enables access to or engagement in healthcare services`         IS TRUE
    `solely or primarily enables an activity specified in regulations under section 62`  IS FALSE
    `displays or otherwise makes available digital content`                              IS TRUE
    `uses artificial intelligence solely or primarily to simulate a personal connection` IS TRUE
    `is specified as an age-restricted platform in regulations under section 62`         IS FALSE

-- The company that actually runs the platform in New Zealand, with no
-- designation anywhere in the picture: the operator under cl 6(1).
`an undesignated controller` MEANS `person in relation to platform` WITH
    name                                                                                  IS "RunsThePlatform Ltd"
    `manages or controls the operations of the platform in New Zealand`                    IS TRUE
    `is an interconnected body corporate of an operator under section 6(1)`                IS FALSE
    `a designation under section 7 is in place for the platform`                           IS FALSE
    `has been designated by the regulator as the operator under section 7`                 IS FALSE
    `the regulator is satisfied that designating this person promotes the purpose`         IS FALSE
    `designating provides certainty about who is and is not an operator`                   IS FALSE
    `designating ensures this Act can be effectively enforced for the platform`            IS FALSE
    `the platform is operated so as to enable a person who is in New Zealand to access it` IS TRUE

-- The same company, once the regulator has designated its overseas parent.
-- It still manages and controls the platform in New Zealand.
`a displaced controller` MEANS `person in relation to platform` WITH
    name                                                                                  IS "RunsThePlatform Ltd (parent designated)"
    `manages or controls the operations of the platform in New Zealand`                    IS TRUE
    `is an interconnected body corporate of an operator under section 6(1)`                IS FALSE
    `a designation under section 7 is in place for the platform`                           IS TRUE
    `has been designated by the regulator as the operator under section 7`                 IS FALSE
    `the regulator is satisfied that designating this person promotes the purpose`         IS FALSE
    `designating provides certainty about who is and is not an operator`                   IS FALSE
    `designating ensures this Act can be effectively enforced for the platform`            IS FALSE
    `the platform is operated so as to enable a person who is in New Zealand to access it` IS TRUE

-- The designated overseas parent. It does not itself manage or control the
-- platform in New Zealand; it is an interconnected body corporate of the company
-- that does, which is what cl 7(1)(b) permits.
`a designated parent` MEANS `person in relation to platform` WITH
    name                                                                                  IS "Parent Inc (designated)"
    `manages or controls the operations of the platform in New Zealand`                    IS FALSE
    `is an interconnected body corporate of an operator under section 6(1)`                IS TRUE
    `a designation under section 7 is in place for the platform`                           IS TRUE
    `has been designated by the regulator as the operator under section 7`                 IS TRUE
    `the regulator is satisfied that designating this person promotes the purpose`         IS TRUE
    `designating provides certainty about who is and is not an operator`                   IS TRUE
    `designating ensures this Act can be effectively enforced for the platform`            IS FALSE
    `the platform is operated so as to enable a person who is in New Zealand to access it` IS TRUE

-- A platform not operated so as to be accessible from New Zealand: cl 8(b)
-- takes it outside the Act even though its controller answers cl 6(1).
`a controller of an inaccessible platform` MEANS `person in relation to platform` WITH
    name                                                                                  IS "NoNZAccess Ltd"
    `manages or controls the operations of the platform in New Zealand`                    IS TRUE
    `is an interconnected body corporate of an operator under section 6(1)`                IS FALSE
    `a designation under section 7 is in place for the platform`                           IS FALSE
    `has been designated by the regulator as the operator under section 7`                 IS FALSE
    `the regulator is satisfied that designating this person promotes the purpose`         IS FALSE
    `designating provides certainty about who is and is not an operator`                   IS FALSE
    `designating ensures this Act can be effectively enforced for the platform`            IS FALSE
    `the platform is operated so as to enable a person who is in New Zealand to access it` IS FALSE

