    `generates a continuously updated stream of digital content`                         IS TRUE
    `displays information about how others have viewed or engaged with user content`     IS TRUE
    `enables a user to view or engage with digital content for a limited period`         IS TRUE
    `has a feature specified as a specified feature in regulations under section 62`     IS FALSE
    `solely or primarily enables person-to-person messages, email, voice or video calls` IS FALSE
    `solely or primarily enables video gaming`                                           IS TRUE
    `solely or primarily enables access to music or podcasts on demand`                  IS FALSE
    `solely or primarily enables access to reviews, technical support, or advice`        IS FALSE
    `solely or primarily enables professional networking or development`                 IS FALSE
    `solely or primarily enables access to or engagement in education services`          IS FALSE
    `solely or primarily enables access to or engagement in healthcare services`         IS FALSE
    `solely or primarily enables an activity specified in regulations under section 62`  IS FALSE
    `displays or otherwise makes available digital content`                              IS TRUE
    `uses artificial intelligence solely or primarily to simulate a personal connection` IS FALSE
    `is specified as an age-restricted platform in regulations under section 62`         IS FALSE

§§ `Machine-evaluated cases`

#EVAL `the service is an age-restricted platform` `a social feed platform`
#ASSERT `the service is an age-restricted platform` `a social feed platform` EQUALS TRUE

-- LQA #1: the excluded-service carve-out in cl 5(2) is attached only to
-- limb (a). A healthcare service that is also an AI companion therefore falls
-- OUT of limb (a) and straight back IN under limb (b).
#EVAL `the service is an age-restricted platform under section 5(1)(a)` `a therapy chatbot`
#EVAL `the service is an age-restricted platform under section 5(1)(b)` `a therapy chatbot`
#ASSERT `the service is an age-restricted platform under section 5(1)(a)` `a therapy chatbot` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the service is an age-restricted platform under section 5(1)(b)` `a therapy chatbot` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the service is an age-restricted platform` `a therapy chatbot` EQUALS TRUE

-- cl 6(1) with no designation in the picture: the controller is the operator.
#ASSERT `the person is an operator under section 6(1)` `an undesignated controller` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the person is the operator of the platform` `an undesignated controller` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `this Act applies to the person as operator of the platform` `an undesignated controller` EQUALS TRUE

-- cl 7(1): the parent qualifies for designation through limb (b), as an
-- interconnected body corporate of a cl 6(1) operator, and cl 7(2)(a) supplies
-- the purpose limb.
#ASSERT `the regulator may designate the person as the operator` `a designated parent` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the person is the operator of the platform` `a designated parent` EQUALS TRUE

-- LQA #6: cl 6(2) makes the designated person "the only operator". A company
-- that manages and controls the platform in New Zealand -- an operator on the
-- face of cl 6(1) -- therefore stops being the operator the moment someone else
-- is designated. Duties in Part 2 attach to "an operator", so the displaced
-- controller owes none while the designation is in place, and the Bill does not
-- say what happens to duties that accrued before it.
#EVAL `the person is an operator under section 6(1)` `a displaced controller`
#EVAL `the person is the operator of the platform` `a displaced controller`
#ASSERT `the person is an operator under section 6(1)` `a displaced controller` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the person is the operator of the platform` `a displaced controller` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `this Act applies to the person as operator of the platform` `a displaced controller` EQUALS FALSE

-- cl 8(b): no New Zealand access, no application, even for a cl 6(1) operator.
#ASSERT `the person is the operator of the platform` `a controller of an inaccessible platform` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `this Act applies to the person as operator of the platform` `a controller of an inaccessible platform` EQUALS FALSE

§§ `Scenario tests -- over-breadth and under-inclusion`

-- SCENARIO A: the tutoring platform is in scope, but through limb (b) only, and
-- only because its AI is used primarily to simulate a personal connection. The
-- variant shows cl 5(1)(b)(iii) doing real work: an AI that teaches rather than
-- befriends leaves the platform out of scope altogether.
#EVAL `the service is an age-restricted platform under section 5(1)(a)` `an ai tutor with a companion avatar`
#EVAL `the service is an age-restricted platform under section 5(1)(b)` `an ai tutor with a companion avatar`
#ASSERT `the service is an excluded service` `an ai tutor with a companion avatar` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the service is an age-restricted platform under section 5(1)(a)` `an ai tutor with a companion avatar` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the service is an age-restricted platform` `an ai tutor with a companion avatar` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the service is an age-restricted platform` `an ai tutor whose ai only teaches` EQUALS FALSE

-- SCENARIO B: the repository is caught by limb (a) on the strength of one
-- specified feature -- cl 5(2)(c), showing an author how others have engaged with
-- their own content -- unless it is characterised as an education service. The
-- outcome turns entirely on that characterisation, which nothing in the Bill
-- settles.
#EVAL `the service has 1 or more specified features` `a scholarly research repository`
#EVAL `the service is an age-restricted platform` `a scholarly research repository`
#EVAL `the service is an age-restricted platform` `a scholarly repository read as education`
#ASSERT `the service is an age-restricted platform` `a scholarly research repository` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the service is an age-restricted platform` `a scholarly repository read as education` EQUALS FALSE

-- LOOPHOLES: both services carry the risk profile the Bill describes, and neither
-- is an age-restricted platform.
#EVAL `the service has 1 or more specified features` `a broadcast-only recommender feed`
#EVAL `the service is an age-restricted platform` `a broadcast-only recommender feed`
#ASSERT `the service has 1 or more specified features` `a broadcast-only recommender feed` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the service is an age-restricted platform` `a broadcast-only recommender feed` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the service has 1 or more specified features` `a social app wrapped in a game` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the service is an age-restricted platform` `a social app wrapped in a game` EQUALS FALSE
